    <html:p>
    Here is Blackburn et all's account:
</html:p>
    <html:p>
    The concept first presented is that of <fr:tree show-metadata="false" expanded="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/hejohns/" title="Johnson He" uri="https://hejohns.github.io/hejohns/" display-uri="hejohns" type="local">Johnson He</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2024</fr:year><fr:month>4</fr:month><fr:day>6</fr:day></fr:date><fr:date><fr:year>2024</fr:year><fr:month>5</fr:month><fr:day>6</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://hejohns.github.io/hejohns-0002/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>hejohns-0002</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/hejohns-0002/</fr:route><fr:title text="bisimulation">bisimulation</fr:title><fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>
    "The basic case":
</html:p><html:p>
    A relation <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Z]]></fr:tex> (to not be confused with the accessibility relations <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex> for
    each Kripke frame) between two Kripke frames <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[M]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[M]]></fr:tex>' is a *bisimulation* iff
    <html:ul><html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[w Z w']]></fr:tex> ⟹ (<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[w]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[w]]></fr:tex>' are elementarily equivalent)
        </html:li>
        <html:li>
            (<html:em>forth</html:em>) <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[w Z w' ∧ w R v ⟹ ∃ v' ∈ M'. w' R' v' ∧ v Z v']]></fr:tex></html:li>
        <html:li>
            (<html:em>backwards</html:em>) <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[w Z w' ∧ w' R' v' ⟹ ∃ v ∈ M. w R v ∧ v Z v']]></fr:tex></html:li></html:ul></html:p><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/hejohns/" title="Johnson He" uri="https://hejohns.github.io/hejohns/" display-uri="hejohns" type="local">Johnson He</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2024</fr:year><fr:month>4</fr:month><fr:day>6</fr:day></fr:date><fr:date><fr:year>2024</fr:year><fr:month>5</fr:month><fr:day>6</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://hejohns.github.io/hejohns-0003/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>hejohns-0003</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/hejohns-0003/</fr:route><fr:title text="bisimilar Kripke frames are elementarily equivalent">bisimilar Kripke frames are elementarily equivalent</fr:title><fr:taxon>moral corollary</fr:taxon></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>
    "Modal formulas cannot distinguish between bisimilar worlds or between bisimilar Kripke frames"

</html:p></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree>.
    A <html:em>simulation</html:em> is where we drop the <html:em>backwards</html:em> condition.
</html:p>
